            "notes": "In most games, I take [Track and Field](item_b3750fe4-e416-42b6-ad9e-fe92c7dcffc5) because we've already invested into our healing field with two powers.   This gives you around 700 HP, which is very powerful in duels or when under pressure, allowing you to use it more often.\n\nIf you're not under pressure, you can add more damage with [Super Visor](item_b3db0ab0-26b4-4d99-893d-175f6726c9e9).\n\nUsually, it's a toss-up between [El-sa'ka Suppressor](item_b4298dd9-9b93-461f-a2e0-843402667100) and [The Closer](item_173c6d0f-dbe6-440e-924f-0ce08189ddce). Pick [El-sa'ka Suppressor](item_b4298dd9-9b93-461f-a2e0-843402667100) against sticky heroes and lots of healing, like Mercy, Moira, or Junker Queen.\n\nSwap [Codebreaker](item_caa96c7e-655f-4d03-9bd9-0f41937fec27) in place of [Talon Modification Module](item_c0ca1795-a3ea-4dc9-ae17-f34122574b3a) if there's a lot of armor, otherwise you can save 3k here.\n\nVery similar logic applies with [Commander's Clip](item_ff7cad01-2065-4908-a2c1-3bdf1458c7a4): You can take either [Commander's Clip](item_ff7cad01-2065-4908-a2c1-3bdf1458c7a4) or [Stockpile](item_a113eb56-9999-4f22-9bd7-18f4dbd00cc2), but [Stockpile](item_a113eb56-9999-4f22-9bd7-18f4dbd00cc2) does about 80% of what [Commander's Clip](item_ff7cad01-2065-4908-a2c1-3bdf1458c7a4) does, so it should NOT be the priority.\n\nLastly, if you're still under a lot of pressure and mostly just need to survive to win, then you can pick [Nebula Conduit](item_476b7040-54c9-4f0c-8283-b4407f6809f8) instead of the damage item for this round.",
